---
import { t } from '@bool/i18n';
import { ROUTES } from '@bool/shared';
import BaseLayout from '@bool/ui/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPageSection from '@bool/ui/sections/LegalPageSection.astro';
import { getHeaderLabels, getFooterLabels } from '../labels';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('pageMeta.privacy.title')}
  description={t('pageMeta.privacy.description')}
  headerLabels={getHeaderLabels()}
  footerLabels={getFooterLabels()}
>
  <LegalPageSection
    headingId="privacy-heading"
    ariaLabel={t('privacy.heading')}
    heading={t('privacy.heading')}
    subtitle={t('privacy.lastUpdated')}
  >
    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Bool, Lda. ("Bool", "we", "us") is the data controller responsible for processing your
      personal data. You can contact us at <a href="mailto:info@bool.pt">info@bool.pt</a> or +351 219
      345 678.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>We collect the following categories of personal data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact form submissions</strong> — name, email address, phone number (optional), and
        message content.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions</strong> — email address.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics data</strong> — anonymised IP address, pages visited, time on site, and browser/device
        information (only with your consent).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Error monitoring data</strong> — technical error logs including browser type and page
        URL (only with your consent).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent</strong> (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR) — for analytics cookies, marketing communications,
        and error monitoring.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) — for responding to contact form inquiries
        and ensuring website security.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To respond to your inquiries submitted via the contact form.</li>
      <li>To send marketing communications you have subscribed to.</li>
      <li>To understand how visitors use our website and improve it (analytics).</li>
      <li>To detect and fix technical errors (error monitoring).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Third-Party Processors</h2>
    <p>
      We share personal data with the following processors, all of which have appropriate data
      processing agreements in place:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics (Google LLC)</strong> — website analytics. IP addresses are anonymised.
        Data may be transferred to the US under Google's EU-US Data Privacy Framework certification.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sentry (Functional Software, Inc.)</strong> — error monitoring. Processes technical error
        data only with your consent. When an error occurs, Sentry may capture a session replay; all text,
        form inputs, and media are masked so no personal data is recorded.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS)</strong> — hosts our contact form and newsletter processing
        endpoints. Data is processed within the EU (eu-west-3 region, Paris).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare Turnstile (Cloudflare, Inc.)</strong> — bot prevention on forms. Processes
        interaction data to verify you are human.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Contact form data</strong> — retained for 12 months after the inquiry is resolved, then
        deleted.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions</strong> — retained until you unsubscribe.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data</strong> — retained for 14 months (Google Analytics default).</li>
      <li><strong>Error monitoring data</strong> — retained for 90 days.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent records</strong> — your consent choices are stored locally on your own device
        (in your browser's local storage), not on our servers. They remain until they expire after 365
        days, until you withdraw consent, or until you clear your browser storage.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>Under GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — request correction of inaccurate data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Erasure</strong> — request deletion of your personal data ("right to be forgotten").
      </li>
      <li><strong>Restriction</strong> — request that we limit processing of your data.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — withdraw previously given consent at any time via the "Cookie
        preferences" link in the footer.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@bool.pt">info@bool.pt</a>.
      We will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      For detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our <a href={ROUTES.cookies}
        >Cookie Policy</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>9. International Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Some of our processors are based in the United States. Transfers are protected by EU Standard
      Contractual Clauses or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, as applicable.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Supervisory Authority</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to lodge a complaint with the Portuguese Data Protection Authority
      (Comissão Nacional de Proteção de Dados — CNPD) at <a
        href="https://www.cnpd.pt"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">www.cnpd.pt</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page
      reflects the most recent revision. Material changes will be communicated via a banner on the
      website.
    </p>
  </LegalPageSection>
</BaseLayout>
